Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Next.js project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package using npm
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the new package and its dependencies

### 2. Analytics Integration
Modified `app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the body tag in the RootLayout component

### Implementation Details
- Followed the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router
- The Analytics component is placed after the children in the body tag as per best practices
- This ensures analytics tracking is initialized for all pages in the application

### Files Modified
- `listing-launch-os/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics component import and usage
- `listing-launch-os/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `listing-launch-os/package-lock.json` - Updated with new package dependencies

### Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully with `npm run build`
- ✅ No TypeScript errors (type checking passed during build)
- ✅ All static pages generated correctly (9/9 pages)
- ✅ Analytics component properly integrated in the root layout

### Next Steps
To enable Web Analytics on Vercel:
1. Navigate to your project's Analytics section in the Vercel dashboard
2. Click the "Enable" button to activate Web Analytics
3. Deploy the application to Vercel
4. Verify tracking by checking browser Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/*`

The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation and is ready for deployment.
